  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23462519"
    description: "Version DOI for v0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  Python research prototype (numpy only). A fail-closed, auditable gate for any
  streaming detector: each 32-value block is checked (NaN, inf, wrong shape,
  non-numeric and, with sequence numbers, missing blocks always latch with a
  reason code), scored by a pluggable scorer (EWMA control chart by default; the
  original weighted residual score S = 0.45·Peak + 0.35·RMS + 0.20·MeanAbs and an
  optional IsolationForest adapter are built in), and latched when S ≥ τ. τ is
  self-calibrated from a warm-up window with an optional bounded drift rule.
  Constant memory per stream and a JSONL audit log of every decision. Real-data
  benchmark on NAB and SMD (REPORTED): the original score does not beat an EWMA
  control chart on NAB and ties on SMD; wrapping a detector in the gate leaves its
  test decisions unchanged, and under fault injection the gate latches every NaN,
  inf and short block that the raw detectors pass or are corrupted by.
keywords:
  - anomaly detection
  - streaming
  - fail-closed
  - guardrail
  - audit log
  - self-calibrated threshold
